    "created_at": "2017-07-14T00:46:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-14T00:46:34Z",
    "body": "So first, note that the spec has a seemingly-unreferenced concept that we could maybe just use:\r\n\r\n> When a new top-level browsing context is created by a script in an existing browsing context [...] and the creation is not **a new start for session storage**, then the session storage area of the origin of that Document must be copied [...]\r\n\r\nSo maybe we should be saying \"is a new start for session storage\"? But see below; I ended up with a different recommendation that removes that paragraph altogether.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI think this new change causes the spec to contradict itself, as there are now two normative statements about how to assign a sessionStorage to a top-level browsing context upon creating it.\r\n\r\nThe existing spec says:\r\n\r\n- Top-level browsing contacts have a 1:1 map: origin -> session storage area. (The spec creates them lazily; that is not important.)\r\n- When creating a Document \"in a browsing context\" that \"has a top-level browsing context\", it does:\r\n  - Let tlbc = document's browsing context's top-level browsing context\r\n  - Let origin = document's origin\r\n  - Set document's session storage area to tlbc.sessionStorageMap[origin].\r\n  - Side note: is \"in a browsing context\" = \"has a browsing context\"? Do any browsing contexts ever not have top-level browsing contexts?\r\n- When creating a new browsing context by \"cloning\" an existing browsing context, it creates a deep clone of a map\r\n  - What is this concept of \"cloning\" a browsing context supposed to mean?\r\n- When a new top-level browsing context is created in the usual ways (script, links, etc.), and the creation is not \"a new start for session storage\", then we create it with a map with one entry: originating Document's origin -> copy of originating Document's session storage.\r\n\r\nNow, what are the modifications introduced in this patch? They seem to duplicate that last requirement, but with a twist about noopener. So I think the spec now contradicts itself.\r\n\r\nTo be clear, the new step's location is better, as it's located during the actual new browsing context creation procedure. But it needs fixing.\r\n\r\nMy recommendation:\r\n\r\n- Remove the \"cloning\" thing.\r\n- Remove the new TLBC paragraph, or replace it with a link to the newly-introduced step.\r\n- Future work: introduce Document's session storage area as a `<dfn>`ed concept; set it during Document creation (have we centralized that yet?) and fix my \"side note\" in the process; formalize the origin -> session storage area map",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
